module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.TensorProduct.Quotient
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Pullback.StalkTensor

/-!
# The local rings of a base change along the spectrum of a quotient

Let `D` be a commutative ring, let `I` be an ideal of `D`, let `Y` be a scheme over `Spec D` and
let

```
W = Y ×_{Spec D} Spec (D ⧸ I)
```

with first projection `pr : W ⟶ Y`. Fix a point `w` of `W` and let `p = pr w`. **If the ideal
generated by `I` in `𝒪_{Y, p}` is contained in the maximal ideal, then the map on local rings
induced by `pr` identifies `𝒪_{W, w}` with `𝒪_{Y, p} / I 𝒪_{Y, p}`.**

No localization survives, in contrast with the general base change
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isLocalization_atPrime_stalk_tensorProduct`: the ring
`𝒪_{Y, p} ⊗[D] D ⧸ I = 𝒪_{Y, p} / I 𝒪_{Y, p}` is already local, being a quotient of a local ring
by an ideal inside its maximal ideal, and the prime at which one would localize is forced to be
its maximal ideal because the map on local rings induced by `pr` is a local homomorphism.

Dividing further by the `N`-th power of the maximal ideal on each side gives the form in which
this is used: if `I 𝒪_{Y, p} ⊆ 𝔪_p ^ N` with `N ≥ 1` then

```
𝒪_{Y, p} / 𝔪_p ^ N ≅ 𝒪_{W, w} / 𝔪_w ^ N.
```

Two base changes of one and the same morphism `Y ⟶ T` along the spectra of two local rings
whose `N`-th truncations agree over `T` can therefore both be compared with the truncated local
ring of a common third base change, which is the use made of this file.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isLocalHom_algebraMap_stalk_of_eq_closedPoint`: the structure map
  `D → 𝒪_{Y, p}` of a scheme over a local ring `D` is a local homomorphism when `p` lies over
  the closed point. This is what makes the hypothesis of the two theorems below checkable.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_ringEquiv_stalk_pullback_of_surjective`: the local ring of
  `Y ×_{Spec D} Spec Λ` at `w` is `𝒪_{Y, pr w} / I 𝒪_{Y, pr w}`, by the map on local rings
  induced by the first projection, for `D → Λ` surjective with kernel `I`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_ringEquiv_quotient_maximalIdeal_pow_stalk_pullback_of_surjective`:
  the truncated form, `𝒪_{Y, pr w} / 𝔪 ^ N ≅ 𝒪_{W, w} / 𝔪_w ^ N`, again induced by the first
  projection.

## Implementation notes

The isomorphisms are stated together with the formula for them on the classes of elements of
`𝒪_{Y, p}`, which is what pins them down: an abstract isomorphism of the two rings would carry
no information and nothing could be transported along it.

The surjection is given as `D → Λ` rather than as `D → D ⧸ I`, because the two sides of the
comparison this file exists for are base changes along two different local rings `D₁`, `D₂` whose
truncations are identified, so the third base change they are both compared with must be taken
along one and the same `Λ`, reached from `D₁` and from `D₂` by two different surjections.

The morphism `Spec Λ ⟶ Spec D` is taken as a variable together with the equation identifying it
with `Spec` of the surjection. That costs nothing at the point of use — the
caller supplies `rfl` — and it keeps the fibre product in the statement a fibre product of two
named morphisms rather than of a morphism and a term, which is what makes the statement usable
at a fibre product that was formed before the quotient map was named.

The hypothesis is an inclusion of the *extended* ideal `I 𝒪_{Y, p}` rather than `I ⊆ 𝔪_D`, which
would not suffice: it is the image of `I` in the local ring of `Y` that has to be small, and
`𝒪_{Y, p}` is a `D`-algebra through a local homomorphism only when `p` lies over the closed point
of `Spec D`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CAW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CAW), clause (5) of which
  needs the resulting comparison of truncated local rings of two base changes
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits IsLocalRing

open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The quotient of a local ring by an ideal inside the maximal ideal is local. -/
private theorem isLocalRing_quotient_of_le_maximalIdeal {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    {J : Ideal R} (hJ : J ≤ maximalIdeal R) : IsLocalRing (R ⧸ J) :=
  have : Nontrivial (R ⧸ J) := Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr
    (ne_top_of_le_ne_top (maximalIdeal.isMaximal R).ne_top hJ)
  .of_surjective' _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective

/-- A localization of `R ⊗[D] D ⧸ I` at the contraction of its maximal ideal, for `R` local and
`I R` inside the maximal ideal of `R`, is already `R ⧸ I R`: the tensor product is a quotient of
the local ring `R`, hence local, and the prime is its maximal ideal because the map `R → S` is a
local homomorphism, so every element outside it is a unit. -/
private theorem exists_ringEquiv_quotient_of_isLocalization_tensorProduct
    {D R S Λ : Type u} [CommRing D] [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [CommRing Λ]
    [Algebra D R] [Algebra D Λ] [IsLocalRing R] [IsLocalRing S]
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (algebraMap D Λ))
    [Algebra (R ⊗[D] Λ) S]
    [IsLocalization (Ideal.comap (algebraMap (R ⊗[D] Λ) S)
      (maximalIdeal S)).primeCompl S]
    (g : R →+* S) [IsLocalHom g]
    (hleft : (algebraMap (R ⊗[D] Λ) S).comp
      Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom = g)
    (hI : (RingHom.ker (algebraMap D Λ)).map (algebraMap D R) ≤ maximalIdeal R) :
    ∃ e : (R ⧸ (RingHom.ker (algebraMap D Λ)).map (algebraMap D R)) ≃+* S,
      ∀ b : R, e (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ b) = g b := by
  set I := RingHom.ker (algebraMap D Λ)
  let eΛ : (D ⧸ I) ≃ₐ[D] Λ :=
    Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective (f := Algebra.ofId D Λ) hsurj
  let e₀ : (R ⧸ I.map (algebraMap D R)) ≃+* R ⊗[D] Λ :=
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivTensorQuot R I).toRingEquiv.trans
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.congr (AlgEquiv.refl (R := D) (A₁ := R)) eΛ).toRingEquiv
  have hmk : ∀ b : R, e₀ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I.map (algebraMap D R)) b) =
      Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom b := by
    intro b
    change (Algebra.TensorProduct.congr (AlgEquiv.refl (R := D) (A₁ := R)) eΛ)
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivTensorQuot R I
          (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I.map (algebraMap D R)) b)) = _
    rw [show Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivTensorQuot R I
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I.map (algebraMap D R)) b) =
      Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom b from rfl]
    simp [Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom]
  have := isLocalRing_quotient_of_le_maximalIdeal hI
  have hsurj₀ : Function.Surjective
      ((e₀ : (R ⧸ I.map (algebraMap D R)) →+* R ⊗[D] Λ).comp
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I.map (algebraMap D R)))) :=
    e₀.surjective.comp Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have : Nontrivial (R ⊗[D] Λ) := e₀.symm.toEquiv.nontrivial
  have : IsLocalRing (R ⊗[D] Λ) := IsLocalRing.of_surjective' _ hsurj₀
  have hgcomp : ∀ b : R,
      algebraMap (R ⊗[D] Λ) S
        ((e₀ : (R ⧸ I.map (algebraMap D R)) →+* R ⊗[D] Λ).comp
          (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I.map (algebraMap D R))) b) = g b := fun b =>
    (congrArg (algebraMap (R ⊗[D] Λ) S) (hmk b)).trans (RingHom.congr_fun hleft b)
  have hlocal : ∀ x : R ⊗[D] Λ, x ∈ maximalIdeal (R ⊗[D] Λ) →
      algebraMap (R ⊗[D] Λ) S x ∈ maximalIdeal S := by
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := hsurj₀ x
    have hb : b ∈ maximalIdeal R := by
      by_contra hb
      exact IsLocalRing.notMem_maximalIdeal.mpr
        ((IsLocalRing.notMem_maximalIdeal.mp hb).map _) hx
    rw [hgcomp b]
    exact map_nonunit g b hb
  have hunits : (Ideal.comap (algebraMap (R ⊗[D] Λ) S)
      (maximalIdeal S)).primeCompl ≤ IsUnit.submonoid (R ⊗[D] Λ) := by
    intro x hx
    rw [IsUnit.mem_submonoid_iff, ← IsLocalRing.notMem_maximalIdeal]
    exact fun h => hx (hlocal x h)
  let eu := IsLocalization.atUnits (R ⊗[D] Λ)
    (Ideal.comap (algebraMap (R ⊗[D] Λ) S) (maximalIdeal S)).primeCompl (S := S) hunits
  exact ⟨e₀.trans eu.toRingEquiv, hgcomp⟩

/-- A ring isomorphism `R ⧸ J ≅ S` of local rings with `J ⊆ 𝔪_R ^ N` descends to an isomorphism
`R ⧸ 𝔪_R ^ N ≅ S ⧸ 𝔪_S ^ N`: an isomorphism of local rings carries the maximal ideal onto the
maximal ideal, so it descends to the `N`-th truncations, and the source of the descended map is
`R ⧸ 𝔪_R ^ N` by the third isomorphism theorem. -/
private theorem exists_ringEquiv_quotient_maximalIdeal_pow_of_ringEquiv_quotient
    {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [IsLocalRing R] [IsLocalRing S]
    (J : Ideal R) (N : ℕ) (hN : 1 ≤ N) (hJ : J ≤ maximalIdeal R ^ N)
    (e : (R ⧸ J) ≃+* S) :
    ∃ e' : (R ⧸ maximalIdeal R ^ N) ≃+* (S ⧸ maximalIdeal S ^ N),
      ∀ b : R, e' (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ b) =
        Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (e (Ideal.Quotient.mk J b)) := by
  have := isLocalRing_quotient_of_le_maximalIdeal (hJ.trans (Ideal.pow_le_self (by omega)))
  have hpow : maximalIdeal S ^ N =
      ((maximalIdeal R ^ N).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)).map (e : (R ⧸ J) →+* S) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_pow, Ideal.map_pow,
      IsLocalRing.map_maximalIdeal_of_surjective (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)
        Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective,
      IsLocalRing.map_maximalIdeal_of_surjective (e : (R ⧸ J) →+* S) e.surjective]
  exact ⟨(DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivQuotOfLE hJ).symm.trans
    (Ideal.quotientEquiv _ _ e hpow), fun _ => rfl⟩

/-- **The structure map `D → 𝒪_{Y, p}` of a scheme over a local ring is a local homomorphism at
a point over the closed point.** The structure map has `Spec` the composite
`Spec 𝒪_{Y, p} ⟶ Y ⟶ Spec D` by `AlgebraicGeometry.specMap_stalkStructureMap`, so the
contraction of the maximal ideal of `𝒪_{Y, p}` along it is the image of the closed point of
`Spec 𝒪_{Y, p}`, which is `p`, hence the closed point of `Spec D`. -/
theorem isLocalHom_algebraMap_stalk_of_eq_closedPoint (D : Type u) [CommRing D] [IsLocalRing D]
    (Y : Scheme.{u}) (f : Y ⟶ Spec (.of D)) (p : Y) (hp : f p = IsLocalRing.closedPoint D) :
    letI : Algebra D (Y.presheaf.stalk p) :=
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of D)).inv ≫ f.appTop ≫
        Y.presheaf.germ ⊤ p trivial).hom.toAlgebra
    IsLocalHom (algebraMap D (Y.presheaf.stalk p)) := by
  let : Algebra D (Y.presheaf.stalk p) :=
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of D)).inv ≫ f.appTop ≫ Y.presheaf.germ ⊤ p trivial).hom.toAlgebra
  rw [IsLocalRing.isLocalHom_iff_comap_closedPoint]
  have hspec : Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap D (Y.presheaf.stalk p))) =
      Y.fromSpecStalk p ≫ f := specMap_stalkStructureMap f p
  have hpt : (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap D (Y.presheaf.stalk p))))
      (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (Y.presheaf.stalk p)) = IsLocalRing.closedPoint D := by
    rw [hspec]
    change f (Y.fromSpecStalk p (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (Y.presheaf.stalk p))) = _
    rw [Scheme.fromSpecStalk_closedPoint]
    exact hp
  exact hpt

/-- **The local ring of `Y ×_{Spec D} Spec Λ` at a point is the local ring of `Y` below it
divided by the ideal generated by the kernel**, for a surjection `D → Λ`. Let `D → Λ` be a
surjective ring homomorphism with kernel `I`, let `f : Y ⟶ Spec D` be a scheme over `D` and let
`w` be a point of the base change `W = Y ×_{Spec D} Spec Λ`, with image `p` under the first
projection `pr`. If the ideal generated by `I` in `𝒪_{Y, p}` lies in the maximal ideal, then
there is a ring isomorphism `𝒪_{Y, p} / I 𝒪_{Y, p} ≅ 𝒪_{W, w}` taking the class of `b` to the
image of `b` under the map on local rings induced by `pr`.

The local ring `𝒪_{W, w}` is a localization of `𝒪_{Y, p} ⊗[D] Λ` at a prime by
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isLocalization_atPrime_stalk_tensorProduct`, and that tensor product is
`𝒪_{Y, p} / I 𝒪_{Y, p}` by `Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivTensorQuot` together with
`Λ = D ⧸ I`. The hypothesis makes it a local ring, and every element outside the prime is then a
unit, because the map on local rings induced by `pr` is a local homomorphism; so the localization
changes nothing. -/
theorem exists_ringEquiv_stalk_pullback_of_surjective
    (D Λ : Type u) [CommRing D] [CommRing Λ] [Algebra D Λ]
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (algebraMap D Λ))
    (Y : Scheme.{u}) (f : Y ⟶ Spec (.of D))
    (q : Spec (CommRingCat.of Λ) ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of D))
    (hq : q = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap D Λ)))
    (w : (pullback f q : Scheme.{u})) :
    letI : Algebra D (Y.presheaf.stalk (pullback.fst f q w)) :=
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of D)).inv ≫ f.appTop ≫
        Y.presheaf.germ ⊤ (pullback.fst f q w) trivial).hom.toAlgebra
    (RingHom.ker (algebraMap D Λ)).map
        (algebraMap D (Y.presheaf.stalk (pullback.fst f q w))) ≤
        maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (pullback.fst f q w)) →
    ∃ e : (Y.presheaf.stalk (pullback.fst f q w) ⧸ (RingHom.ker (algebraMap D Λ)).map
        (algebraMap D (Y.presheaf.stalk (pullback.fst f q w)))) ≃+*
        (pullback f q : Scheme.{u}).presheaf.stalk w,
      ∀ b : Y.presheaf.stalk (pullback.fst f q w),
        e (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ b) = ((pullback.fst f q).stalkMap w).hom b := by
  subst hq
  intro hI
  let : Algebra D (Y.presheaf.stalk
      (pullback.fst f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap D Λ))) w)) :=
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of D)).inv ≫ f.appTop ≫ Y.presheaf.germ ⊤
      (pullback.fst f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap D Λ))) w)
      trivial).hom.toAlgebra
  obtain ⟨ψ, hleft, -, hloc⟩ :=
    exists_isLocalization_atPrime_stalk_tensorProduct D Λ Y f w
  let : Algebra (Y.presheaf.stalk
      (pullback.fst f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap D Λ))) w) ⊗[D] Λ)
      ((pullback f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap D Λ)))
        : Scheme.{u}).presheaf.stalk w) := ψ.toAlgebra
  have : IsLocalization (Ideal.comap ψ (maximalIdeal
      ((pullback f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap D Λ)))
        : Scheme.{u}).presheaf.stalk w))).primeCompl
      ((pullback f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap D Λ)))
        : Scheme.{u}).presheaf.stalk w) := hloc
  have : IsLocalHom ((pullback.fst f
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap D Λ)))).stalkMap w).hom :=
    (pullback.fst f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap D Λ)))).toLRSHom.prop w
  exact exists_ringEquiv_quotient_of_isLocalization_tensorProduct hsurj
    ((pullback.fst f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap D Λ)))).stalkMap w).hom
    hleft hI

/-- **The truncated local rings of a base change along `Spec Λ ⟶ Spec D` agree with those of the
source**, for a surjection `D → Λ`. In the situation of
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_ringEquiv_stalk_pullback_of_surjective`, if the ideal generated by the
kernel in `𝒪_{Y, p}` lies in `𝔪_p ^ N` with `N ≥ 1`, then
`𝒪_{Y, p} / 𝔪_p ^ N ≅ 𝒪_{W, w} / 𝔪_w ^ N`, by the map on local rings induced by the first
projection.

The isomorphism `𝒪_{Y, p} / I 𝒪_{Y, p} ≅ 𝒪_{W, w}` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_ringEquiv_stalk_pullback_of_surjective` carries the maximal ideal onto
the maximal ideal, being an isomorphism of local rings, so it descends to the `N`-th
truncations; the source is then `𝒪_{Y, p} / 𝔪_p ^ N` by the third isomorphism theorem. -/
theorem exists_ringEquiv_quotient_maximalIdeal_pow_stalk_pullback_of_surjective
    (D Λ : Type u) [CommRing D] [CommRing Λ] [Algebra D Λ]
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (algebraMap D Λ))
    (Y : Scheme.{u}) (f : Y ⟶ Spec (.of D))
    (q : Spec (CommRingCat.of Λ) ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of D))
    (hq : q = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap D Λ)))
    (w : (pullback f q : Scheme.{u})) (N : ℕ) (hN : 1 ≤ N) :
    letI : Algebra D (Y.presheaf.stalk (pullback.fst f q w)) :=
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of D)).inv ≫ f.appTop ≫
        Y.presheaf.germ ⊤ (pullback.fst f q w) trivial).hom.toAlgebra
    (RingHom.ker (algebraMap D Λ)).map
        (algebraMap D (Y.presheaf.stalk (pullback.fst f q w))) ≤
        maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (pullback.fst f q w)) ^ N →
    ∃ e : (Y.presheaf.stalk (pullback.fst f q w) ⧸
          maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (pullback.fst f q w)) ^ N) ≃+*
        ((pullback f q : Scheme.{u}).presheaf.stalk w ⧸
          maximalIdeal ((pullback f q : Scheme.{u}).presheaf.stalk w) ^ N),
      ∀ b : Y.presheaf.stalk (pullback.fst f q w),
        e (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ b) =
          Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (((pullback.fst f q).stalkMap w).hom b) := by
  intro hI
  obtain ⟨e₁, he₁⟩ :=
    exists_ringEquiv_stalk_pullback_of_surjective D Λ hsurj Y f q hq w
      (hI.trans (Ideal.pow_le_self (by omega)))
  obtain ⟨e₂, he₂⟩ :=
    exists_ringEquiv_quotient_maximalIdeal_pow_of_ringEquiv_quotient _ N hN hI e₁
  exact ⟨e₂, fun b => by rw [he₂ b, he₁ b]⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
